<% content_for :title, "Percentage Calculator — whizwheel" %>

<%#
  Percentage calculator (spec issue #31) — a multi-mode calculator (ARCHITECTURE.md
  §3.2 spec:v1), regenerated for iteration-0005 from the spec + BLEND (DESIGN.md). A
  required `mode` selects one of five percentage operations; only the inputs that mode
  names are shown, and the single result key it returns (value | percent | base) drives
  the hero answer. Two-up on desktop — an input column + a results panel (≈380px 1fr,
  DESIGN.md §3 layout grid) — collapsing to one stacked column on mobile (mobile-first).

  Submit model: a plain server-rendered <form> posting inputs[...] to the §4 endpoint
  over Turbo (Accept: turbo-stream → create.turbo_stream.erb replaces #result in place).
  It works with NO JS — the server validates exactly the selected mode and re-renders the
  result region. Stimulus is pure polish (DESIGN.md §0.5): it reveals only the active
  mode's fields (disabling the rest so they aren't posted) and lifts the active states.

  Mode-picker presentation (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker") — always a native radio
  <fieldset>/<legend> posting a single-select inputs[mode]; presentation chosen by count +
  label length:
    • Main picker — FIVE modes, every label multi-word → the selectable option list
      (.mode-option): one bordered, divided container of full-width rows, each a radio
      glyph + a bold mode name + a one-line helper. (N ≥ 4 or any multi-word label ⇒
      option list — never a wrapping pill row, never a <select> as the primary picker.)
    • Direction sub-toggle (change mode) — N = 2, short labels (Increase | Decrease) ⇒
      the segmented control (the connected horizontal track, DESIGN.md §4).

  Spacing (DESIGN.md §3 — targets, not minimums): stacked fields → space-y-5 (Stacked);
  mode → fields → submit, the major blocks → mt-8 (Section); column gutters / card
  padding → gap-8 / p-7–p-8 (Layout).
%>

<header class="max-w-2xl">
  <p class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-accent">Math</p>
  <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-[-0.035em] text-ink">Percentage Calculator</h1>
  <p class="mt-3 text-[15px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
    Five percentage operations in one place — what is P% of a number, what percent one
    number is of another, percent-of-what, the difference between two numbers, and a
    percent increase or decrease. Every answer is computed server-side.
  </p>
</header>

<div class="mt-8 grid grid-cols-1 gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[380px_1fr]">
  <%# ── Input column ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────── %>
  <section class="rounded-[18px] border border-border bg-surface p-7 shadow-[0_10px_34px_rgba(150,110,80,0.12)] sm:p-8">
    <%= form_with url: "/calculators/percentage", scope: :inputs, method: :post,
          data: { controller: "percentage" } do |f| %>

      <%# Main mode picker — the selectable option list (DESIGN.md §4 "Mode picker"):
          five multi-word modes ⇒ ONE bordered, divided container of full-width rows,
          NOT N wrapping chips and NOT a <select>. A native radio <fieldset>/<legend>
          posts inputs[mode]; each radio is visually-hidden (peer sr-only) and paired to
          a styled <label for>. peer:checked paints the active row with no JS, and the
          row's leading radio glyph (.mode-option::before) is the non-colour active cue
          (DESIGN.md §6). Each row carries the mode name + a one-line helper. %>
      <fieldset>
        <legend class="field-label">Mode</legend>
        <div class="mt-3 overflow-hidden rounded-[13px] border border-border-input divide-y divide-rule">
          <% [
               ["percent_of",      "Percent of a number",   "What is P% of a number"],
               ["what_percent",    "What percent",          "What percent one number is of another"],
               ["percent_of_what", "Percent of what",       "A number is P% of what whole"],
               ["difference",      "Percentage difference", "The percent difference between two numbers"],
               ["change",          "Increase / decrease",   "Apply a P% increase or decrease to a number"]
             ].each_with_index do |(value, name, helper), i| %>
            <div>
              <%= f.radio_button :mode, value,
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { percentage_target: "modeInput", action: "percentage#select" } %>
              <%= f.label :mode, value: value,
                    class: "mode-option",
                    data: { percentage_target: "modeOption", mode: value } do %>
                <span class="text-sm font-semibold text-ink"><%= name %></span>
                <span class="text-xs text-muted"><%= helper %></span>
              <% end %>
            </div>
          <% end %>
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <%# Per-mode fields. Each block declares the modes it serves via
          data-percentage-modes; Stimulus shows only the active mode's blocks and disables
          the inputs in the rest so they aren't submitted. The no-JS baseline submits every
          field, and the server validates only the selected mode's required set, ignoring
          inputs the mode doesn't name. Stacked tier — space-y-5. %>
      <div class="mt-8 space-y-5">
        <%# V1 — required by every mode. %>
        <div data-percentage-target="field"
             data-percentage-modes="percent_of what_percent percent_of_what difference change">
          <%= f.label :v1, "Value (V1)", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_v1" %>
          <%= f.number_field :v1, id: "inputs_v1", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                placeholder: "0", class: "field-input mt-1.5" %>
        </div>

        <%# V2 — what_percent, difference. %>
        <div data-percentage-target="field"
             data-percentage-modes="what_percent difference">
          <%= f.label :v2, "Value (V2)", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_v2" %>
          <%= f.number_field :v2, id: "inputs_v2", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                placeholder: "0", class: "field-input mt-1.5" %>
        </div>

        <%# Percent — percent_of, percent_of_what, change. The % rides beside its field as
            a unit affix on the Affix tier (gap-2, DESIGN.md §3). %>
        <div data-percentage-target="field"
             data-percentage-modes="percent_of percent_of_what change">
          <%= f.label :percent, "Percent (P)", class: "field-label", for: "inputs_percent" %>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= f.number_field :percent, id: "inputs_percent", step: "any", inputmode: "decimal",
                  placeholder: "0", class: "field-input" %>
            <span class="text-sm font-bold text-label" aria-hidden="true">%</span>
          </div>
        </div>

        <%# Direction — change only. N = 2 short labels ⇒ the segmented control: a native
            radio <fieldset>/<legend> over a connected horizontal track, the chosen half
            lifted to surface white (DESIGN.md §4). %>
        <fieldset data-percentage-target="field" data-percentage-field="change"
                  data-percentage-modes="change">
          <legend class="field-label">Direction</legend>
          <div class="mt-1.5 flex gap-1 rounded-[11px] border border-border-input bg-bg p-1">
            <% [["increase", "Increase"], ["decrease", "Decrease"]].each_with_index do |(value, text), i| %>
              <%= f.radio_button :direction, value,
                    checked: i.zero?,
                    class: "peer sr-only",
                    data: { action: "percentage#selectDirection" } %>
              <%= f.label :direction, text, value: value,
                    class: "direction-pill",
                    data: { percentage_target: "directionPill" } %>
            <% end %>
          </div>
        </fieldset>
      </div>

      <%# Submit — Section tier above; the primary coral button (DESIGN.md §4). %>
      <%= f.submit "Calculate",
            class: "mt-8 w-full cursor-pointer rounded-[13px] bg-primary px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-surface shadow-sm transition-opacity hover:opacity-90 focus:outline-none focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-accent" %>
    <% end %>
  </section>

  <%# ── Results panel (the Turbo target; aria-live so the answer is announced) ── %>
  <section id="result" aria-live="polite">
    <%= render "calculators/result", calc: nil %>
  </section>
</div>
